      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 530 and 976. To make this easier, I'll break down 976 into 1000 minus 24.\n\nSo, the problem becomes 530 multiplied by (1000 - 24).\n\nNext, I'll distribute the multiplication: 530 times 1000 minus 530 times 24.\n\nCalculating 530 times 1000 gives me 530,000.\n\nThen, I'll calculate 530 times 24. Breaking this down further, 530 times 20 is 10,600, and 530 times 4 is 2,120. Adding these together gives 12,720.\n\nFinally, I'll subtract 12,720 from 530,000 to get the final result.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **530** and **976**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nLet's break down **976** to make the multiplication simpler:\n\\[\n976 = 1000 - 24\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Apply the Distributive Property\nNow, multiply **530** by each part of the broken-down number:\n\\[\n530 \\times 976 = 530 \\times (1000 - 24)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 530 \\times 1000 - 530 \\times 24\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n1. **Calculate \\(530 \\times 1000\\):**\n\\[\n530 \\times 1000 = 530{,}000\n\\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(530 \\times 24\\):**\n\\[\n530 \\times 24 = 530 \\times (20 + 4) = (530 \\times 20) + (530 \\times 4)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 10{,}600 + 2{,}120 = 12{,}720\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Subtract the Two Results\n\\[\n530{,}000 - 12{,}720 = 517{,}280\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{517,\\!280}\n\\]",
