      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 861 and 965. To make this easier, I'll break down 965 into 1000 minus 35.\n\nSo, the problem becomes 861 multiplied by (1000 - 35).\n\nNext, I'll distribute 861 across the subtraction: 861 * 1000 minus 861 * 35.\n\nCalculating 861 * 1000 gives me 861,000.\n\nNow, I'll calculate 861 * 35. Breaking this down further, 35 is 30 plus 5.\n\nSo, 861 * 30 is 25,830, and 861 * 5 is 4,305.\n\nAdding those two results together gives 25,830 + 4,305 = 30,135.\n\nFinally, I'll subtract 30,135 from 861,000 to get the final product: 861,000 - 30,135 = 830,865.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **861** and **965**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   861 \\times 965 = 861 \\times (1000 - 35)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Distribute the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   861 \\times 1000 - 861 \\times 35\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate Each Part Separately:**\n\n   - **First Part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 1000 = 861,\\!000\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Second Part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 35 = 861 \\times (30 + 5) = (861 \\times 30) + (861 \\times 5)\n     \\]\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 30 = 25,\\!830\n     \\]\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 5 = 4,\\!305\n     \\]\n     \n     \\[\n     25,\\!830 + 4,\\!305 = 30,\\!135\n     \\]\n\n4. **Subtract the Second Part from the First Part:**\n\n   \\[\n   861,\\!000 - 30,\\!135 = 830,\\!865\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{830,\\!865}\n   \\]",
