      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 947 and 988. To make this easier, I'll break down 988 into 1000 minus 12.\n\nSo, the problem becomes 947 multiplied by (1000 - 12).\n\nNext, I'll distribute the multiplication: 947 times 1000 minus 947 times 12.\n\nCalculating 947 times 1000 gives me 947,000.\n\nThen, I'll calculate 947 times 12. Breaking this down further, 947 times 10 is 9,470 and 947 times 2 is 1,894. Adding these together gives 11,364.\n\nFinally, I'll subtract 11,364 from 947,000 to find the final product.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **947** and **988**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can simplify the multiplication by breaking down **988** into more manageable parts:\n\\[\n988 = 1000 - 12\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Apply the Distributive Property\nNow, multiply **947** by each part separately:\n\\[\n947 \\times 988 = 947 \\times (1000 - 12)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 947 \\times 1000 - 947 \\times 12\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n1. **Calculate \\(947 \\times 1000\\):**\n\\[\n947 \\times 1000 = 947{,}000\n\\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(947 \\times 12\\):**\n\\[\n947 \\times 12 = 947 \\times (10 + 2) = 947 \\times 10 + 947 \\times 2\n\\]\n\\[\n= 9{,}470 + 1{,}894 = 11{,}364\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Subtract the Two Results\n\\[\n947{,}000 - 11{,}364 = 935{,}636\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{935,\\!636}\n\\]",
